      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like aosp/4368094 already keeps `maxrss` and `cmaxrss` in one unit across exec and mixed page sizes: `setmax_mm_hiwater_rss()` converts each mm\u0027s high-water mark to kernel pages with `mm_kernel_pages()`, in that mm\u0027s own page size, before it reaches `signal-\u003emaxrss` from `exec_mmap()`, `do_exit()` or `getrusage()`. `getrusage()` then converts kernel pages to kB, since `kernel/sys.c` doesn\u0027t opt into `\u003clinux/p3s_user_pages.h\u003e`.\n\nAs far as I can see, the only difference here is that a 4KB process\u0027s `ru_maxrss` is no longer rounded up to the next 16KB, i.e. it can be up to 12KB lower. `rusage_p3s` in aosp/4367986 allows 4MB of slack, so it should pass either way.\n\nWould it be OK to drop this patch, rather than change the unit of the `signal_struct` fields? If the rounding matters somewhere, could the commit message say where?",
